EXT. MOUNTAIN PASS - GUN POSITION - DAWN

Snow. Rock. A barricade of sandbags.

CAPTAIN YEVGENY ROSTOV, 40s, fur collar, studies the valley through binoculars. Beside him, LIEUTENANT BEATRIZ SALAZAR, 30s, cleans a sidearm. SERGEANT KOFI MENSAH, 40s, shoulders a crate. CORPORAL DALTON PIKE, 20s, shivers. PRIVATE ANNELIESE VOGT, 19, chews her lip. And a boy soldier, TOMAS, 16, grips a radio.

                    YEVGENY
Quiet.

Wind. A distant engine.

                    BEATRIZ
They're early.

                    YEVGENY
They always are.

Kofi sets down the crate. Pries it open. Grenades.

                    KOFI
Dawn special.

                    DALTON
Can't feel my fingers.

                    KOFI
Then you'll feel nothing when they hit.

                    ANNELIESE
That's not funny.

                    KOFI
It's not meant to be.

Tomas holds up the radio. His voice cracks.

                    TOMAS
Captain! Sir! They say two columns!

                    YEVGENY
Which flank?

                    TOMAS
Both!

Yevgeny lowers the binoculars. The engine grows.

                    BEATRIZ
We hold.

                    KOFI
^
We hold.

Both look at each other. A grim, small smile.

A SHELL screams in. White geyser. The barricade rattles. Snow rains down on all of them.

Dalton throws himself flat. Anneliese screams. Tomas drops the radio. Yevgeny stands, completely still, watching the ridge.

                    YEVGENY
Positions!

They scramble.
